  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[strava-for-office-chairs]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <title>
      <Value><![CDATA[Strava for Office Chairs]]></Value>
    </title>
    <tagline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Kudos for 4 km to the coffee machine. On wheels.]]></Value>
    </tagline>
    <demoFeatures>
      <Value><![CDATA[Roll Segment
Kudos Spin
Swivel PR
Lumbar Mode]]></Value>
    </demoFeatures>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[Quantify all sitting | Every roll, swivel and lean-back in the Nordics, tracked. Nobody asked the chairs.
Tour de Office | A 21-stage race through the open-plan floor. The mountain stage is the canteen door sill.
Chair-to-chair social network | Chairs follow each other, give kudos and judge each other's wheels. Humans optional.
Monetise the swivel | Premium: see who swivelled past your desk. The free tier just feels the breeze.
Olympic chair sprint by 2032 | Lobby for office chair racing as a discipline. We already have a lycra budget.
One wellness KPI for management | A single number for the whole office's activity. Rolling to the fridge counts double.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Desk to coffee segment | As a developer, I want a timed segment to the coffee machine so that my only cardio is ranked.
Kudos for staying put | As an office chair, I want kudos for eight hours stationary so that loyalty is finally a sport.
Stolen chair tracking | As a chair owner, I want GPS on my chair so that I can prove Marketing took it after the town hall.
Privacy zone: Friday bar | As an employee, I want a privacy zone at the Friday bar so that the data stays as fuzzy as I am.
Standing desk doping control | As a rival, I want standing desk users flagged so that 'elevation gain' means something.
Lean-back personal best | As a senior, I want my recline angle logged so that I can beat my record during estimation.
Roll and talk | As a PM, I want 'walk and talk' replaced with 'roll and talk' so that nobody has to stand up.
Rate my human | As an office chair, I want to rate my human so that the one who eats kebab at the desk gets feedback.
Physio integration | As a physiotherapist, I want the posture data so that I can say 'yes, I can tell' with graphs.
Home office segment | As a remote worker, I want my dining chair to count so that my back pain is at least ranked.
Broken wheel category | As a chair with one stuck wheel, I want my own category so that going in circles counts as a route.
Local legend badge | As a receptionist, I want the Local Legend badge for most swivels so that people finally fear me.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[Swivel counter | Counts full rotations. More than three in a row triggers 'thinking or bored?'.
Gas lift elevation gain | Logs every centimetre up. And the slow, sad sinking through the day.
King of the Coffee Machine | A crown for the fastest roll from desk to coffee. Spilling is a time penalty.
Squeak recognition | Identifies your chair by its squeak. The whole office already can.
Wheel health check | Reports hair, crumbs and one LEGO brick per wheel.
Commute tracking | Logs the journey from your desk to the meeting you are already late for.
Carpet mode | Adjusts the effort score by surface. Carpet is the new altitude training.
Drafting detection | Catches you being towed by a colleague. Disqualified, but beautiful.
Post-lunch slump graph | Activity from 1 to 2:30 pm. A flat line with one small sigh.
Armrest clearance alert | Warns you before the armrest meets the edge of the desk. Again.
Flyby replay | Watch who rolled past your desk without saying hi.
Rest day reminder | Recommends a rest day. For the chair. You still have to come in.
Route art | Draw a Christmas tree on the floor plan with your route. Takes one afternoon. Billable.
Chair bell | Ding ding in the corridor. Pedestrians must give way.
Weekly effort email | 'You rolled 312 m this week. That is 0.7% of a marathon. Well done.'
Group ride to lunch | Synchronised departure at 11:29. The peloton forms at the lift.]]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[Chair logged a marathon overnight | 42 km while the office was empty. Either GPS drift or the cleaners are having fun.
Robot vacuum tops the leaderboard | Not a chair. Refuses to be removed. Has 40 followers and a sponsor.
Swivel counter overflow | User spun for an entire Teams call. Counter went negative. User went pale.
Elevation: minus 4 cm per hour | Chair sinks, app logs 'descent'. User is now at keyboard height with a personal best.
Segment goes through a wall | Fastest route to the canteen crosses Meeting Room 3, mid-meeting. Two users tried.
Kudos sent to the wrong chair | All meeting room chairs are identical. One of them is now an influencer.
Activity not recorded | User rolled all the way to the printer and it didn't count. User went back and did it again.
Auto-pause in status meetings | App detects no signs of life and pauses the activity. Works as designed?]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[The sensor is a phone under the seat | An old phone and gaffer tape from 2022. It still gets calls from somebody's grandma.
Distance is measured in 'desks' | The desks changed size in the office move. Nobody recalibrated. Nobody will.
Floor plan predates the renovation | Half the segments finish inside a wall that became a phone booth in 2021.
Leaderboard is a shared Excel | KOM_final_NEW_use_this.xlsx. Three people have it open. One of them since May.
Hardcoded: wheels = 4 | Every chair has five. The fix was estimated at 'an afternoon' in 2023.
Auth is the sticker on the chair | You are whoever the label says you are. The label maker has been missing for years.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[CEO Request: Can my chair win? | It has leather armrests and has never moved. 'Just find a category.'
CEO Request: Link it to timesheets | 'If we can track the chairs, we can track the hours.' The room went very quiet.
CEO Request: Chairs with AI | 'Smart chairs. I don't know what they do. That's your job.' Said from a moving taxi.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[If it's not logged, you never rolled.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[Track every roll, swivel and slow sink of the gas lift. Compete on segments like Desk to Coffee Machine. Give kudos. Never stand up.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Start rolling]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Segments that matter | Desk to Printer. The Canteen Sprint. The legendary Door Sill Climb by Meeting Room 2. Live leaderboards.
Every swivel counts | Our sensor logs rotations, recline and sighs per hour. Your physiotherapist gets a copy. Sorry.
Kudos culture | Rolled four metres to ask something you could have sent on Teams? Somebody will call it a strong effort.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[I took King of the Coffee Machine from Finance. They took my chair. It is war.
My chair did 2 km last week. I did 300 steps. We are both proud.
The gas lift sinks 4 cm a day. The app calls it 'descent'. I call it Tuesday.
We lost a junior on the Door Sill Climb. All fine. A local legend now.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[Free for chairs with five wheels. Premium (DKK 39 a month) for chairs with four wheels and a sad one.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© Strava for Office Chairs. Roll responsibly. Pedestrians in the corridor must give way.]]></Value>
    </siteFooterLine>
